## Metadata
Title: Find the Missing Cross Words
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-01-04
Description: A 13-wide diamond (the same outline as No. 1) with a black cross in the centre (shown as _) lettered in white "IT'S READS BOTH WAYS" (the first word is blotted; IT'S is the likely reading). No solution was printed anywhere, so the letters are unknown: every square of the puzzle is written as "." and the clues have no answers.
Incomplete: no printed solution has been found, so the grid's letters and the answers are unknown.
Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1914-01-04, p. 80


